y from the action result, leaving only status code and optional error info. The error will still contain the missing alias name which will probably be enough info to diagnose the issue.The action information could be added back in the follow-up once this class is a bit clearer.\r\n","I think this is reasonable, thanks"],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/indices/alias/TransportIndicesAliasesAction.java","id":35298,"created_at":"2024-04-03T17:10:49Z","original_position":93,"side":"RIGHT","position":93,"submitted_on_commit":"481ee9d8cd64812b96a7fff5d7d8f64ce4161a01","diff_hunk":"@@ -233,14 +245,18 @@ protected void masterOperation(\n                         throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Unsupported action [\" + action.actionType() + \"]\");\n                 }\n             }\n+\n+            Arrays.stream(concreteIndices).map(Index::getName).forEach(resolvedIndices::add);\n+            actionResults.add(AliasActionResult.build(resolvedIndices, action, numAliasesRemoved));","submitted_line":250},"generatedCommentsNodes":[]}],"coveredGroundTruth":0,"uncoveredGroundTruth":1,"coveredMatchable":26,"uncoveredMatchable":23,"timing":39518,"tokensIn":10214,"tokensOut":985}